 [17592186442840 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442834 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442840 1079 #uuid "e7049d2d-fc9f-5f20-8e5c-02896d997034" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442841 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442837 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442841 1069 "q-132362" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442841 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442841 1071 "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}),$ what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442841 1072 #uuid "0dc4b9d8-5da7-5586-a518-10322d637373" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442841 1074 "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{{\\lambda }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}),$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442842 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442838 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442842 1069 "q-138321" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442842 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442842 1071 "The time $X,$ in days, between two doses of medication in a patient's treatment can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(6).$ If a dose has just been taken by the patient, what is the average time until the next dose?" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442842 1072 #uuid "358a711e-17d9-56a3-a7f2-d4538d452099" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442842 1074 "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(6).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =6,$ which means that $6$ doses are taken each day. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{day}=4\\,\\text{h}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next dose is $4$ hours." 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442843 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442839 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442843 1069 "q-138314" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442843 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442843 1071 "The time $X,$ in weeks, between two grandkids visiting their grandma can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(7).$ If a grandkid has just visited their grandma, what is the average time until the next grandkid visits their grandma?" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442843 1072 #uuid "7ced14e8-8144-5a90-a159-85ee1ea70744" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442843 1074 "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(7).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =7,$ which means that grandkids visit their grandma at an average rate of $7$ visits per week. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{week}=1\\,\\text{day}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next grandkid's visit is $1$ day." 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442844 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442840 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442844 1069 "q-132627" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442844 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442844 1071 "The time $X,$ in minutes, between two visitors entering a restaurant can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{2}).$ If a visitor has just entered the restaurant, what is the average time until the next visitor enters?" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442844 1072 #uuid "bbd9b202-0edb-5252-b84c-96bc38834bd7" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442844 1074 "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{2}).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2},$ and\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{min}=2\\,\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next visitor is $2$ minutes." 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442845 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442848 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442845 1062 #uuid "5cd54c92-39ad-5b9a-a09b-fe3547af99e6" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442845 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442843 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442846 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442845 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442846 1062 #uuid "778e6bc3-396f-57e9-ad00-0591e91cecbb" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442846 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442844 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442847 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442846 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442847 1062 #uuid "d0c54f8f-efb1-5756-b356-6ea276ef3ad3" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442847 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442841 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442848 1062 #uuid "d1a1ba80-2f4c-549a-969a-7ffdffc5fabd" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442848 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442842 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442849 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442847 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442849 1062 #uuid "ec507f4e-7ad4-574b-b220-b028ea07092f" 13194139534890 17592186045417 true] [17592186442849 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167078 13194139534890 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-80633357-7af9-5c1a-9cb9-41c3ac411d31" 17592186442816 "answer-05547d8f-b729-55a9-8be3-036d66839167" 17592186442817 "answer-08fdcd7a-935f-5b89-954e-94cfe53551b5" 17592186442818 "answer-13aa5558-5072-53e7-bd58-cf7c7ba5a133" 17592186442819 "answer-2520da57-e0e2-58df-b3cf-ec9420890983" 17592186442820 "answer-2fe74356-49b8-543c-8d6e-d896f6be8ab6" 17592186442821 "answer-